  answer="After a Breathe session in the Mindfulness app, Apple Watch shows your heart rate on the Summary screen. You can find it later in the Health app on iPhone: Heart, Heart Rate, Show More Heart Rate Data, then Breathe. To compare before and after, you need an app that keeps a reading from both ends of the session."
  sections={[
    {
      h2: 'What Apple Watch records during a Breathe session',
      paras: [
        "Apple's Mindfulness app on the Watch has two sessions, Reflect and Breathe. Apple's user guide says that once you complete a Reflect or Breathe session, \"your heart rate appears in the Summary screen.\" Apple's heart rate guide adds that, by default, the Watch monitors your heart rate for the Heart Rate app, workouts, and Breathe and Reflect sessions.",
        "You choose a session length between 1 and 5 minutes. The pace lives in Settings on the Watch, under Mindfulness, then Breath Rate, which sets the number of breaths per minute. The same screen sets haptics to None, Minimal or Prominent. You can change all of it from the Apple Watch app on iPhone too, under My Watch, then Mindfulness.",
